{"tool_name":"graph_peak_caller","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"Graph_Peak_Caller","home":"https://github.com/uio-bmi/graph_peak_caller","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"Tool for calling transcription factor peaks on graph-based reference genomes using ChIP-seq data.","addition_date":"2019-05-19T07:52:30Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:Graph_Peak_Caller","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Biomedical Informatics Research Group (BMI)","typeEntity":"Division","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.mn.uio.no/ifi/english/research/groups/bmi/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Haplotype mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0487"},{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"},{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Graph Peak Caller","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1006731","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 Grytten et al.Graph-based representations are considered to be the future for reference genomes, as they allow integrated representation of the steadily increasing data on individual variation. Currently available tools allow de novo assembly of graph-based reference genomes, alignment of new read sets to the graph representation as well as certain analyses like variant calling and haplotyping. We here present a first method for calling ChIP-Seq peaks on read data aligned to a graph-based reference genome. The method is a graph generalization of the peak caller MACS2, and is implemented in an open source tool, Graph Peak Caller. By using the existing tool vg to build a pan-genome of Arabidopsis thaliana, we validate our approach by showing that Graph Peak Caller with a pan-genome reference graph c